  "user": "Fine. Back to that charge — what do I do next?",
  "answer": "The next step is for you to tell me what happened with the charge. I can't see the earlier eligibility results from this session, so I'll re-run the check once we've picked the transaction and reason.\n\nYour account ACC-1005 shows two settled card payments to TechMart Online for the same amount:\n\n- **TX-0402**, 14 July 2026, €240.00\n- **TX-0401**, 20 July 2026, €240.00\n\nIf one of these is the charge you mean, that could point to a duplicate charge. Please tell me:\n\n1. Which transaction you're disputing, or whether it's a different charge (there is also CityParking, TX-0403, €35.50, on 1 September).\n2. What happened. For example: you were charged twice for one purchase, you didn't authorise the payment, the goods or services didn't arrive, or the service wasn't provided as agreed.\n\nOnce you describe it, I'll check eligibility for the matching reason code. I won't open a dispute until that check passes and you confirm.",
